body:
Hello, I think I encounter the same issue.

I have an index with the following mapping:
```json
            "properties": {
                "folders": {
                    "type": "text",
                    "fields": {
                        "keyword": {
                            "type": "keyword",
                            "ignore_above": 256
                        }
                    }
                }
}
```

I have the following script:
```json
{
    "script": {
        "lang": "painless",
        "source": " ctx._source.folders.replaceAll(f -> f.replace(params.oldFolderPath, params.newFolderPath)); "
    }
}
```

This script was working in 7.15.x and is not working in 7.16.x with the following error:
```json
{
                    "type": "illegal_argument_exception",
                    "reason": "failed to execute script",
                    "caused_by": {
                        "type": "script_exception",
                        "reason": "runtime error",
                        "script_stack": [
                            "f -> f.replace(params.oldFolderPath, params.newFolderPath)); ",
                            "^---- HERE"
                        ],
                        "script": "update-folder-path-in-resources",
                        "lang": "painless",
                        "position": {
                            "offset": 32,
                            "start": 32,
                            "end": 93
                        },
                        "caused_by": {
                            "type": "illegal_argument_exception",
                            "reason": "cannot convert function reference [this::lambda$synthetic$0] to a non-functional interface [java.util.function.UnaryOperator]"
                        }
                    }
```
I'm guessing this is the same bug but not really sure.

@TheFireCookie It's the same bug.  It's nice to have a repro for `UnaryOperator`.

In [`LambdaTests.java`](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/master/modules/lang-painless/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/painless/LambdaTests.java)
```java
    public void testUnaryOperator() {
        assertEquals("doremi", exec("List lst = ['abc', '123']; lst.replaceAll(f -> f.replace('abc', 'doremi')); lst.get(0);"));
        assertEquals("doremi", exec("def lst = ['abc', '123']; lst.replaceAll(f -> f.replace('abc', 'doremi')); lst.get(0);"));
    }
```
